===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|telt}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|teld||tent}}, from {{etyl|gml|en}} {{m|gml|telt}},<ref>[http://ordnet.dk/ods/opslag?opslag=telt&submit=S%F8g Etymology] in [[:w:da:ODS|ODS]]</ref> perhaps via or influenced by {{etyl|da|en}} {{m|da|telt}}.<ref>{{R:Webster 1913|tilt}}</ref> Cognates include German {{m|de|Zelt||tent}}, Old Norse {{m|non|tjald||tent}} (whence also archaic Danish {{m|da|tjæld||tent}}). More at {{l|en|teld}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[canvas]] covering for carts, boats, etc. {{defdate|1450}}
# Any covering overhead; especially, a [[tent]].
#: {{rfquotek|Denham}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cover with a tilt, or awning.

